                <pb facs="1047" n="927" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg927"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bowen to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Manager of the Bermudez Company informed Mr. Bowen to-night his superintendent,
                    American citizen, is held prisoner at the Lake, and closely guarded by
                    Venezuelan soldiers. Mr. Bowen will protest to-morrow morning, and request
                    immediate release, stating he does so while waiting instructions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
